    },
    [264] = {
        {
            id = 276003,
            score = 143,
            author = "44749",
            text = "I have to say - this is one of the most beautifully well-written, and (unlike Yuriv's tomb) unforgettable quests that I've come across in almost two years of playing WoW.",
            date = "2008-04-23T01:38:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=264#comments:id=276003",
        },
        {
            id = 716583,
            score = 111,
            author = "360859",
            text = "This is actually one of my favorite quests in the game, mostly because it's one of the few quests, if not only, whose ending seems to lack the sort of redemptive accomplishment common to tragedy-ridden quests.\n\nSimilar quests that come to mind with happier endings than beginnings (or at least some sense of redemption) would be the Mor'Ladim (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=225) line in Duskwood, the Shady Rest Inn (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=1282) line in Dustwallow Marsh, and Tirion Fordring's (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=5742) line in Eastern Plaguelands.\n\nThis quest, on the other hand, lacks anything that could be considered redeeming. A woman wants you to return a pendant to the grave of her deceased husband, who died trying to protect her and her children from the one thing they ultimately succumbed to. Were it up to her, she'd rather forget he ever existed. Such an errand might possibly have proven cathartic, but even this is blunted and ineffective.\n\nIn the end you realize that Yuriv has passed beyond memory and will be forgotten forever. A very terrible fate for a husband and father who died trying to protect his family.\n\nA sad quest with an even sadder ending, one of those kind that makes you end up hating the world somehow.",
            date = "2009-05-15T01:31:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=264#comments:id=716583",
        },
        {
            id = 428087,
            score = 67,
            author = "DeviousDVO",
            text = "This quest never fails to make me feel melancholy.",
            date = "2008-11-02T01:01:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=264#comments:id=428087",
        },
        {
            id = 1563180,
            score = 56,
            author = "821910",
            text = "This gave me the shivers and made me wonder what's going on here really.\n\nClarice is in Mulgore; the gravestone's on another continent. It has been vandalised with the word BETRAYER. One could ASSUME it was her who did it, but...that seems pretty effin' stupid do me. Why would she call him 'betrayer'?\n\nWhat I want to know is this: since it likely was not his wife, who scratched that onto his tombstone?\n\nThe wording is important here. Clarice absolutely does not say he betrayed her. She says he DITCHED her. Her big revenge against him, until you leave the necklace, is obviously leaving his grave alone the way she was left alone. (I'm not passing judgment on who's virtuous or a jerk here; I'm explaining how the lady feels, so chillax. XD)\n\nSo who's calling him a traitor? Who put those candles there?\n\nSomething freaky's going on here, but I'm not sure what. Could he have sold out to the Scourge under duress or torture? Was he like Rivendare, and he kind of got tempted and strayed bigtime?\n\nWhat the hell happened here?",
            date = "2011-11-04T21:56:22-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=264#comments:id=1563180",
        },
        {
            id = 892906,
            score = 45,
            author = "292744",
            text = "I loved this quest. Personally, I really find this sort of tragic tale very entertaining. And besides that, I think that this underlines one of the things most misinterpreted about the Forsaken, especially in regards to Deld's comment: the Plague changed them. Most of them turned their back on the Light. They are bitter, and hateful. All in all, they are probably one of the most contreversial and \"see it from different points of view\" kinds of things in the whole Warcraft universe.\n\nGreat stuff, really, for the kind of lore-jocky I am.",
            date = "2009-11-16T21:29:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=264#comments:id=892906",
        },
    },
