            score = 31,
            author = "zaber",
            text = "If you are level 70 you can do this solo even without stealth. Helps to be a mage to blink past a few \"tight spots\".\n\nEnter BRD, go through the locked door on your left, continue straight to the \"highway\", take a right and follow the hall to Incendius, melt his face, loot corpse, dance happy jig, disenchant BOP drop (if you can), continue straight and go up the ramp, avoid mobs by walking on the railing most fo the way. At the top fo the ramp go through the doorway and go to the left, take the next left into the Cofffer Room. Blink past the boss and the dog so you are standing against the Dark Coffer. Attack and kill the dog and ignore the boss until the dog is dead. At level 70 you should resist all or most of the bosses spells. Kill the boss, loot and dance again, DE, walk to the edge of the room (stand about where the boss was standing), adjust your camera angle so you can click the picture on the wall and read the caption n the picture to find where the NPC is that you need to kill to get the Dark Coffer Key. Backtrack to wherever that mobs is and kill him to get the key, then return to the Coffer Room, open the Dark Coffer, loot contents, hearth out to Orgrimmar or Ironforge... spam the trade channel til you sell the \"enchant\" or get ignored by everyone on your server.\n\nIf you happen to get ignored by everyone on the server, pay Blizzard to do a server transfer to another. Repeat as needed.\n\n:-P",
            date = "2007-03-30T20:55:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4482#comments:id=59882",
        },
    },
    [4483] = {
        {
            id = 59879,
            score = 37,
            author = "zaber",
            text = "If you are level 70 you can do this solo even without stealth.  Helps to be a mage to blink past a few \"tight spots\".\n\nEnter BRD, go through the locked door on your left, continue straight to the \"highway\", take a right and follow the hall to Incendius, melt his face, loot corpse, dance happy jig, disenchant BOP drop (if you can), continue straight and go up the ramp, avoid mobs by walking on the railing most fo the way.  At the top fo the ramp go through the doorway and go to the left, take the next left into the Cofffer Room.  Blink past the boss and the dog so you are standing against the Dark Coffer.  Attack and kill the dog and ignore the boss until the dog is dead.  At level 70 you should resist all or most of the bosses spells.  Kill the boss, loot and dance again, DE, walk to the edge of the room (stand about where the boss was standing), adjust your camera angle so you can click the picture on the wall and read the caption n the picture to find where the NPC is that you need to kill to get the Dark Coffer Key.  Backtrack to wherever that mobs is and kill him to get the key, then return to the Coffer Room, open the Dark Coffer, loot contents, hearth out to Orgrimmar or Ironforge... spam the trade channel til you sell the \"enchant\" or get ignored by everyone on your server.\n\nIf you happen to get ignored by everyone on the server, pay Blizzard to do a server transfer to another.  Repeat as needed.\n\n:-P",
            date = "2007-03-30T20:52:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4483#comments:id=59879",
        },
        {
            id = 4660,
            score = 16,
            author = "182",
            text = "This CAN be enchanted through the trade window. Rogues and Druids can stealth run the BRD coffer for the Burning Essence, and give it to anyone once they turn in the quest for the arcanum.",
            date = "2006-11-26T14:06:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4483#comments:id=4660",
        },
        {
            id = 172556,
            score = 13,
            author = "Vesper",
            text = "with thanks to Zaber's comments I just did this a couple of times to help out the tanks for the illidan encounter. I would like to add the following:\n- you can have multiple Burning Essence in your bag so you can reset the instance over and over (well untill 5x max per hour) until you have all the needed Burning Essence.\n- you can have multiple Lesser Arcanum of Resilience in your bags aswell (they don't stack though)\n\nI just sent all my Libram's through the mail and went flying back and forth to Redridge to pick them up.\n\nThis information below from another site (source (http://wow.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?witem=11751;page=1;howmany=50#1165864703213263922)) helped me out aswell.\nThe list of Dark Key holders and where they can be found are:\nDark Keeper Offgut West Garrison - room with Angerforge\nDark Keeper Bethek Patrols near Coffer room\nDark Keeper Vorfalk Grim Guzzler Tavern\nDark Keeper Zimrel Arena; upper seating area\nDark Keeper Uggel Top of ramp in Golem Room w/Fineous\nDark Keeper Pelver Domicile room (storeroom in center)\n\nAll but 2 are fairly easy to do.\nBethek spawns almost instantly outside the Coffer room, so be prepared.\nVorfalk is surrounded by patrons in the Grim Guzzler. To get to him, you have to pull the patrons around him, 1 by 1, with the Dark Iron Ale.\nJust make sure you kill the patron before they drink it, as it's limited in supply.\nAfter all that, the Burning Essence is still a 50% drop, so you may need a few attempts before you get it.",
            date = "2007-10-21T06:48:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4483#comments:id=172556",
        },
        {
            id = 6791,
            score = 0,
            author = "6684",
            text = "stealth running the instance isnt all that simple though, the dogs can see through stealth from a decent distance and taking some of the groups of mobs can be challenging even for a well geared player. having imp sap is definitely a plus",
            date = "2006-12-05T22:18:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4483#comments:id=6791",
        },
        {
            id = 164525,
            score = 0,
            author = "84526",
            text = "Can you use this infinite times or is it only once?",
            date = "2007-10-08T00:04:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4483#comments:id=164525",
        },
    },
    [4484] = {
        {
            id = 686031,
            score = 14,
            author = "67353",
            text = "These enchants are no longer useable in the trade-screen. They will soulbind if used on an BoE item as well. This was done to nerf twinks further  in the 3.1 patch.",
            date = "2009-04-20T10:08:22-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4484#comments:id=686031",
        },
        {
            id = 144510,
            score = 12,
            author = "43040",
            text = "Good to know info:\nUnlike the Aldor or Scryer enchanting items. Which bind to you when you get them and then bind the item you use it on to you also.\n\nOnly the Arcanum binds to you. Using the Arcanum on an item does not bind the item to you.\n\nSo... +8 stam on a twink head piece is something to think about.",
            date = "2007-08-26T20:04:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4484#comments:id=144510",
        },
        {
            id = 2218,
            score = 10,
            author = "jason",
            text = "This is actually quite useful for a paladin.  Consider what the +8 Int does for us.  First, +8 Int.  Assuming at 60 the paladin formula for spell crit is:\n\n[INT/29.5?]%\n\nThis gives us .27% crit chance for 8 Int.\n\nNow, also assume that paladins have Divine Intellect, and Blessing of Kings, that increases the 8 int to about 9.6 (or 9.68, however, they do the math) int.  Assuming they round up, that's 10 int.\n\nCompare this to the ZG enchant, which give us 10 Stamina, 24 healing, and 7 defense.  Assuming at this point that defense is all but useless for a current end-game raiding paladin, it comes down to +healing and stamina and more mana and spell crit.\n\nWith two enchants, you have the following totals:\n\nZG: 48 +healing, 200 health\nLIbram: 20 Int (assuming BoK and DI talent), which gives us .54% spell crit, ~300 mana\n\nConsidering the limited number of ZG enchants you can get these days, +8 int doesn't look that bad.",
            date = "2006-10-24T13:50:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4484#comments:id=2218",
        },
        {
            id = 1316000,
            score = 7,
            author = "Aluminum",
            text = "These will probably be popular for the BoA helms once most bigger guilds start hitting level 20.\n\nAssuming they work on them that is, all the other available enchants require an item level and not character level.",
            date = "2011-01-30T15:54:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4484#comments:id=1316000",
        },
        {
            id = 819467,
            score = 6,
            author = "413549",
            text = "Anyone who is turning these in for Insane in the Membrane (http://www.wowhead.com/?achievement=2336)\nWill notice that this wont award any reputation to shen'dralar\nwhat is rly odd if you ask from me\n\nedit:\n\nQuest is now obsolete as it no longer exist ingame",
            date = "2009-08-22T09:43:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4484#comments:id=819467",
        },
    },
    [4512] = {
        {
            id = 2355,
            score = 39,
            author = "Banduin",
            text = "Use the empty jars on the oozes after you kill them.  Just make sure to loot them first.",
            date = "2006-10-28T17:02:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4512#comments:id=2355",
        },
        {
            id = 129506,
            score = 24,
            author = "McKizz",
            text = "You will need to travel to Felwood for this quest.\n\nYou will receive a box with the jars in them. If you are having inventory troubles (full inventory, etc) leave them in the box until you are ready to do the quest. After you open the box, you will receive 2 sets of 6 jars. One set for the Tainted Ooze, one set for the Cursed Ooze.\n\nThe Tainted Ooze can be found at the two ponds in Jaedenar. The coordinates are 40, 59 and 40, 55 for those two ponds.\n\nThe Cursed Ooze can be found just south of there at two other ponds. The coordinates for those two ponds are 40, 67 and 40, 71.\n\nAfter you kill the Oozes, be sure to loot them. Then, select their dead \"body\" and use the appropriate container (Cursed or Tainted, depending on what you just killed) to fill the jar with ooze.\n\nWhen you are finished, you will need to fly back to Ironforge to turn in the quest to Laris Geardawdle in the Hall of Explorers.",
            date = "2007-07-30T23:43:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4512#comments:id=129506",
        },
        {
            id = 195310,
            score = 17,
            author = "serpentea",
            text = "A funny note for anyone who happened to quest in Menethil...\n\n\"I helped a lady in Menethil find her bag not too long ago--it was eaten by oozes.\" the quest giver says this refering to http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=470\n\nI found this to be slightly humorous...",
            date = "2007-12-03T08:53:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4512#comments:id=195310",
        },
        {
            id = 133222,
            score = 14,
            author = "Bayer",
            text = "This is the follow-up quest : http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=4513",
            date = "2007-08-06T12:44:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=4512#comments:id=133222",
        },
        {
            id = 42411,
