        },
        {
            id = 391004,
            score = 22,
            author = "161675",
            text = "This is a repeatable quest available to anyone in AV.  The items disappear from your inventory when the match is completed.\n\nThese items are turned in at our base (Frostwolf Keep) to the wing commanders.  After a set number of turn-ins the commanders will launch an air strike.\n\nGuse = needs 90 Stormpike Soldier's Flesh\nJeztor = needs 60 Stormpike Lieutenant's Flesh\nMulverick = needs 30 Stormpike Commander's Flesh\n\nWhen they have the required number of items, they will shout something and the blue ? above their heads will go away.  -- Talk to them again to begin the airstrike. --\n\nYou have to be revered or higher to be able to tell them to take flight, otherwise the only option you get is to get a beacon and take it to the field of strife.  Luckily even if someone has taken the beacon, another player can still go talk to the wing commanders and tell them to take flight.\n\nFor the wing commanders to be at our base, we first need to find them & talk to them so they can run back.  They are lying on the floor in three seperate locations: Mulverick is at the Dun Baldar North Tower, Guse is at Icewing Bunker & Jeztor is in a shack at the Stormpike lumberyard (if you are looking at the map there are two little purple house icons slightly northeast of IWB, she is in the lower one) at 53, 27 if you have coordinates.\n\nAside from rep & an air assualt with enough turn ins, there is also a small amount of bonus honor awarded if the wing commanders make it back to the base safely.  Since it seems like every little bit of honor counts, I like to make sure I wake up Guse and Jez asap.\n\nOnce they are back at our base, they will be standing in front of what looks like a flight point at the top part of our base.  You can use your Frostwolf Insignia http://www.wowhead.com/?item=17690 to recall (ie be ported) back to our base & they will be standing directly to your right when you recall.  The Frostwolf Insignia is a reward from the quest Proving Grounds http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=7161 which is available from an NPC in the Alterac Mountains at level 51.\n\nThere are usually a small number of \"runners,\" players who like to loot as many bodies as possible and then recall to turn in the items.  -- Please do not loot bodies unless you plan on doing the turn-ins. --",
            date = "2008-09-28T16:32:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6827#comments:id=391004",
        },
        {
            id = 940578,
