    [6847] = {
        {
            id = 6239575,
            score = 1,
            author = "MinXwasTaken",
            text = "For the Korrak's Revenge version of this quest, see https://www.wowhead.com/quest=57640 / https://www.wowhead.com/quest=57641 . This page refers to the original version of this quest before Alterac Valley was remade, and has since been removed from the regular AV Battleground.\n\nThis quest is still doable in 2025 during Korrak's Revenge while Anniversary is up!\n\nGrab the quest from Master Ryson, go to Winteraxe Cave (beyond the western bridge at Snowfall Graveyard), grab Master Ryson's All-Seeing Eye on the platform in the middle of the cave (It's interactable on the floor, no mob kills required), you will receive a 15 minute buff.\n\nNow run manually all the way back to Master Ryson. Mount, Stealth, Death etc. cancel your buff. One thing worth mentioning that I noticed was that after I got the eye and buff I used my Frostwolf Insignia to teleport back and it removed my buff, but dropped the interactable eye at my feet, in front of my faction's keep. So depending on the current state of battle it might be worthwhile for you to teleport to your keep, pick up the eye from there and walk to Master Ryson that way.\n\n/way 56 50 Master Ryson (Inside Cave)\n\nIf you die or any other player picked it up before you it is unobtainable again during this Korrak's Revenge. You can keep the quest for the next run though and then immediately go to the cave to grab the eye.\n\n- This quests awards 150 base rep with your Frostwolf Clan/Stormpike Guard faction, but since it is only available during Anniversary you will get 165 Rep minimum (you can get up to 195 with Blessing of the Bronze Dragonflight and the 10% Spirit of Sharing Buff if you turn this quest in during the 1 week where Pilgrim's Bounty and Anniversary overlap)\n- This quest CAN be repeated infinitely each day(once a match only) which makes for a pretty decent AV faction rep farm, depending on how fast your queue time for Korrak's Revenge is\n\nP.S. The trolls in the cave are max level elites so ideally you'll want speed/healing/defensive buffs ready to use. I'd recommend running in with those buffs utilized, grabbing the eye, running out and then using a deaggro ability if you can, otherwise just run past the trolls outside until they deaggro.",
            date = "2025-12-05T13:44:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6847#comments:id=6239575",
        },
        {
            id = 3466,
